{"name":"Oat Cake","hex":"#e1cab3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Widely cultivated cereal grass, typically Avena sativa.","Any of the numerous species, varieties, or cultivars of any of several similar grain plants in genus Avena."]},{"part":"Prepositional phrase","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of OAT."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oat"},{"term":"cake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich, sweet dessert food, typically made of flour, sugar, and eggs and baked in an oven, and often covered in icing.","A small mass of baked dough, especially a thin loaf from unleavened dough."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Coat (something) with a crust of solid material.","To form into a cake, or mass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oatcake","blocks":[{"text":"An oatcake is a type of flatbread similar to a cracker or biscuit, or in some versions takes the form of a pancake. They are prepared with oatmeal as the primary ingredient, and sometimes include plain or wholemeal flour as well. Oatcakes are cooked on a griddle or baked in an oven."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Oatcakes_%281%29.jpg/330px-Oatcakes_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oatcake","wikidata":"Q3347905"},{"title":"Oat","blocks":[{"text":"The oat, sometimes called the common oat, is a species of cereal grass (Avena) grown for fodder and for its seed, which is known by the same name. Oats appear to have been domesticated as a secondary crop, as their seeds resembled those of other cereals closely enough for them to be included by early cultivators. Oats tolerate cold winters less well than cereals such as wheat, barley, and rye, but need less summer heat and more rain, making them important in areas such as Northwest Europe that have cool, wet summers. They can tolerate low-nutrient and acid soils. Oats grow thickly and vigorously, allowing them to outcompete many weeds, and compared to other cereals are relatively free from diseases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/AvenaSativa3.jpg/330px-AvenaSativa3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oat","wikidata":"Q12104"},{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pound_layer_cake.jpg/330px-Pound_layer_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake","wikidata":"Q13276"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Making_oat_cakes_-_The_costume_of_Yorkshire_%281814%29%2C_plate_IX%2C_opposite_21_-_BL.jpg/500px-Making_oat_cakes_-_The_costume_of_Yorkshire_%281814%29%2C_plate_IX%2C_opposite_21_-_BL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Making_oat_cakes_-_The_costume_of_Yorkshire_%281814%29%2C_plate_IX%2C_opposite_21_-_BL.jpg/1280px-Making_oat_cakes_-_The_costume_of_Yorkshire_%281814%29%2C_plate_IX%2C_opposite_21_-_BL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Making_oat_cakes_-_The_costume_of_Yorkshire_%281814%29%2C_plate_IX%2C_opposite_21_-_BL.jpg/500px-Making_oat_cakes_-_The_costume_of_Yo